changes:
When an earlier group already built a group, so that group's agents commit nothing, a whole-repository unit-test run decides what happens:
  - if it passes, the build records an empty `test:` and `feat:` pair carrying the unit trailer and `Already-built: yes`, and the unit goes on to the checks and review;
  - if it fails, the unit stops with the existing 'the branch holds no tests and implementation pair' message.

These cases make no empty commit:
  - the unit-test run fails or finds a flake; its output is saved as unit-test feedback and counted as a check failure;
  - the environment is broken; the unit is blocked as an environment problem instead;
  - the branch has a real tests commit but no implementation after it;
  - the first group has nothing on the branch at all;
  - `per_group_commits` is off.
